      "content": "it's such a massive weight to carry, feeling like the world is this thin, flickering thing that nobody else can see. it's actually getting harder to function in normal crowds because the 'static' is everywhere. like, if a person is about to have a panic attack or even just make a bad decision, i see these jagged, electric-looking pulses around them. it's not just visual, it's like i can feel the tension in the air before the event even happens. since you mentioned the Orch-OR model, does that mean my brain is actually detecting these quantum states in real-time? i'm trying to figure out if there's a way to 'smooth out' the noise so i can actually tell the difference between minor fluctuations and something truly significant.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
